  "notes": "{貫|つらぬ}く has both a physical sense (piercing through) and a figurative sense (persisting in). The figurative sense is more common in everyday usage.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for the thing being pierced or the principle being upheld\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{貫|つらぬ}いている indicates an ongoing state of maintaining a position or belief.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS (figurative):\n- {信念|しんねん}を{貫|つらぬ}く: stick to one's beliefs\n- {意志|いし}を{貫|つらぬ}く: carry through one's will\n- {沈黙|ちんもく}を{貫|つらぬ}く: maintain silence\n- {姿勢|しせい}を{貫|つらぬ}く: keep one's stance\n\nINTENSIFIED FORM:\n{貫|つらぬ}き{通|とお}す adds emphasis, meaning to see something through to the very end despite obstacles.",
